  "question": {
    "text": "Let&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mi>NaCl</mi></msub></math>&nbsp;and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mi>BaSO</mi></msub><mn>4</mn></msub></math>, be the conductances (in S) measured for saturated aqueous solutions of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>NaCl</mi></math>&nbsp;and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>B</mi><mi>a</mi><mi>S</mi><msub><mi>O</mi><mn>4</mn></msub></math> respectively, at a temperature T. Which of the following is false?"
